leanne_sales: Heads-up — Aurora Systems POC kickoff tomorrow. They want streaming SDK-based inference with model-initiated tool/function calls (webhook-style), and strictly validated structured JSON output for invoice extraction. Also asking about Dedicated vs Hosted pricing, SOC2 + KMS requirements, and IP allowlist/VPC options. Can someone stand by with a short SDK example and a one-pager runbook?

alex_devex: On it. Quick clarifying q's: what's the expected peak QPS and avg tokens per response? Are tool invocations synchronous (model waits for webhook) or async (fire-and-forget)? Also: p50 latency SLO target?

leanne_sales: Peak ~80 qps, avg ~120 tokens/response. Tool calls roughly 1 in 5 responses and they want the model to wait for webhook results (sync). Latency target p50 <120ms, p95 <300ms. Client is enterprise, SOC2 required, KMS for key management.

alex_devex: Ok. For streaming + sync tool calls we recommend the streaming SDK + function calling pattern. Minimal Node example (conceptual):

```js
// stream + tool call (pseudo)
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY, routing: { mode: 'dedicated' } });
const stream = client.stream({ model: 'redwood-rtf-1', streaming: true, functions: [invoiceToolSpec] });
stream.on('data', chunk => process.stdout.write(chunk));
stream.on('function_call', async (call) => {
  // call customer's webhook synchronously
  const res = await fetch(call.endpoint, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(call.args) });
  const json = await res.json();
  stream.resumeWithFunctionResult(json);
});
```

For structured output validation: require the model to emit a top-level `invoice` field matching this schema: {"invoice_id":"string","total_cents":"number","line_items":[{"desc":"string","qty":"number","unit_cents":"number"}]}. Validate at the edge and reject nonconforming responses.

Also for latency: use dedicated routing, enable KV prefix caching, and set batching limits (max_batch_size=8, max_wait_ms=10) to keep p50 low while preserving throughput.

sam_solutions: Pricing notes: Hosted per-token math will swing the operational cost; DMing a quick calc based on your QPS and token averages. For Dedicated — baseline reserved cluster for this scale usually starts in the low-mid five figures/mo (depends on GPU type & commit). We can propose a hybrid: reserved baseline + burst hosted to control cost. I'll send concrete numbers in a DM and loop finance for an enterprise quote. :+1:

ben_infra: Security checklist: IP allowlist + customer CIDR -> requires either Private deployment or Dedicated with VPC peering and a NAT-to-customer arrangement. On-prem KMS or customer-managed KMS is supported but needs a short integration window. SOC2 attestation available — I can drop the PDF into the deal folder. Ask Aurora to provide the security questionnaire now; give us the SF contact to map requirements to configuration items.

alex_devex: I'll assemble a short runbook + a small test harness (pytest + mock webhook) and push to the presales repo today. Will include: sample streaming test, function-call mock, structured-output schema validation script, and a perf checklist (batching, cache, routing). Ping me for repo access.

leanne_sales: Awesome, thanks everyone. I'll upload their security questionnaire and schedule Wed 10am sync. @sam_solutions I'll expect your DM with numbers so we can prep the proposal. :rocket:
